WEBVTT

00:16.014 --> 00:16.944
Karada!

00:17.314 --> 00:19.174
Come back! Karada!

00:19.514 --> 00:20.774
Come back!

00:22.854 --> 00:23.914
Karada!

00:30.364 --> 00:31.654
I'm sorry.

00:41.874 --> 00:43.034
Karada...

01:27.754 --> 01:29.244
We need to talk.

01:35.124 --> 01:38.114
Something reached for but cannot be grasped...

01:39.764 --> 01:43.464
Something that strays from that hand,
going far away...

01:44.964 --> 01:49.464
People will always pursue such things.

01:50.344 --> 01:53.774
And before long, become lost.

01:59.744 --> 02:04.314
This is our story of one such summer.

02:22.604 --> 02:24.074
Living for the Day
After Tomorrow

02:24.074 --> 02:27.744
Living for the Day
After Tomorrow
The children's graffiti

02:27.744 --> 02:28.174
Living for the Day
After Tomorrow

02:28.514 --> 02:32.174
That has blossomed on the asphalt

02:32.944 --> 02:36.574
Shimmers in the waves of heat

02:37.424 --> 02:40.254
And has begun to walk

02:40.394 --> 02:45.224
At that promised hill

02:45.224 --> 02:48.854
That no one knows

02:49.394 --> 02:54.104
Encounter the miraculous time called "today"

02:54.104 --> 02:58.874
That comes only once - feel it

02:58.874 --> 03:03.044
Chase the flowing clouds

03:03.044 --> 03:07.384
Even now, they seem in your grasp

03:07.384 --> 03:11.754
A premonition, heart beating with excitement

03:11.754 --> 03:16.384
A destiny that has begun to move

03:16.494 --> 03:20.864
So bright that you awaken

03:20.864 --> 03:24.894
Hotter even than the morning sun

03:25.134 --> 03:29.034
Sparkling without end

03:29.374 --> 03:36.674
Embraced in the season of light

03:39.184 --> 03:43.484
The Signpost

03:43.724 --> 03:45.444
Well, how'd it go?

03:45.954 --> 03:48.984
You asked, right? About the postcard?

03:49.854 --> 03:52.054
What did Hiro say?

04:02.504 --> 04:03.374
The hell are you doing?!

04:03.374 --> 04:05.174
You're so frickin' gloomy!

04:05.174 --> 04:08.044
Since you've been back, all you've done
is mope around not saying a word.

04:08.044 --> 04:11.534
You're not a little kid anymore,
so at least answer when you're spoken to!

04:13.884 --> 04:15.114
Kanocho
TETSUMASA AMINO

04:15.114 --> 04:16.814
Kanocho
TETSUMASA AMINO
What's this supposed to mean?!

04:17.124 --> 04:20.284
This is postmarked from Kanocho!

04:20.394 --> 04:21.824
"Visiting relatives," my ass!

04:21.954 --> 04:24.684
Iokawa's here, isn't she?! Where is she?

04:25.164 --> 04:26.424
Well?!

04:26.794 --> 04:29.664
My sister is... not here.

04:30.664 --> 04:34.294
Not in this house. And not in this city.

04:36.104 --> 04:37.294
She left.

04:38.244 --> 04:41.174
"Left"? Where to?

04:43.944 --> 04:45.514
Where did she go?!

04:45.514 --> 04:47.574
Hey! Say something!

04:50.624 --> 04:53.914
After all that, he said
he didn't know where she was...

04:54.454 --> 04:58.254
And that she might not come back at all.

05:00.264 --> 05:02.294
She goes missing...

05:02.294 --> 05:04.534
Then they've found her.

05:04.534 --> 05:06.904
Then she's at her relatives' house...

05:06.904 --> 05:08.764
Then she's left somewhere.

05:09.634 --> 05:12.304
What the heck is going on?!

05:12.674 --> 05:14.914
I don't even know what I'm supposed to do!

05:14.914 --> 05:16.004
Ow, ow, ow!

05:17.244 --> 05:18.834
What are you doing?!

05:21.654 --> 05:24.384
I knew my brother was an idiot,

05:24.384 --> 05:26.944
but I don't remember him being
a sniveling whiner!

05:27.654 --> 05:29.724
You don't know what you're "supposed to do"?

05:29.724 --> 05:32.324
There's only one thing that you
WANT to do, right?!

05:32.324 --> 05:35.294
You're the one's who's always running off
without thinking things through, right?!

05:36.934 --> 05:37.964
Sis...

05:37.964 --> 05:41.524
What did you say when you came
barging into my house?

05:41.874 --> 05:43.994
What happened to "living for the moment"?!

06:15.404 --> 06:17.374
Now just wait, Tetsumasa!

06:17.374 --> 06:22.314
You cause me such worry and when I think
you've finally come home, you act like THIS!

06:22.314 --> 06:24.004
Wait right there, Tetsumasa!

06:24.414 --> 06:25.744
Tetsumasa!

06:26.214 --> 06:28.374
Are you even listening? Tetsumasa!

06:51.174 --> 06:53.974
I'll find you and show them all, lokawa.

06:55.214 --> 06:56.734
May I sit here?

06:57.184 --> 06:58.774
Yeah. Go ahead.

07:05.584 --> 07:07.124
K-Kotomi!

07:07.124 --> 07:10.024
What's with you? That's being
a little TOO surprised!

07:11.464 --> 07:14.394
What're you doing today?
Shopping or something?

07:14.394 --> 07:16.224
But you're mom's not with you...

07:16.994 --> 07:18.434
So? Where're you going?

07:18.434 --> 07:20.164
Uh...

07:23.374 --> 07:25.634
I... I'm trying to live for the moment!

07:28.974 --> 07:30.244
The heck is that?

07:30.244 --> 07:32.904
Who'd you steal that line from?!

07:34.914 --> 07:38.374
What are you even doing here, Kotomi?
You taking a trip or something?

07:40.924 --> 07:45.364
I'm going to a sleepover at my
elementary school teacher's place.

07:45.964 --> 07:51.164
Over and over it's been, "You're in Kanocho now,
you're close, come on by!"

07:51.504 --> 07:54.064
A schoolteacher? Bleh.

07:54.734 --> 07:58.204
Well, Teach really came through for me,
in school and out.

07:58.204 --> 08:00.764
I can't just say no...

08:01.674 --> 08:05.044
You're changing trains, right?
This is where I get off.

08:05.044 --> 08:06.534
Okay, bye!

08:14.594 --> 08:16.924
Can't say I can help you...

08:17.164 --> 08:20.934
I think it would've been two or three days ago.
You don't remember her?

08:20.934 --> 08:23.864
A lot of people pass through here every day.

08:23.964 --> 08:27.494
Oh. Thank you very much.

08:32.144 --> 08:33.904
Fess up, you!

08:37.814 --> 08:39.304
She's missing?!

08:41.954 --> 08:43.654
Kotomi, you're way too loud!

08:43.654 --> 08:48.094
But this girl... This little girl is?!

08:48.094 --> 08:51.094
That's bad, right? Like, BAD bad?!

08:51.094 --> 08:53.894
I mean, look! There's been lots of
funny stuff happening recent-

08:54.564 --> 08:56.794
You're way off base!

08:56.794 --> 09:01.994
To make a long story short, she was
apparently back home a few days ago.

09:02.974 --> 09:04.134
But...

09:05.044 --> 09:06.664
Did you tell the police?

09:08.374 --> 09:10.244
Her family would have done that already, right?!

09:10.244 --> 09:12.114
Then why not just wait to hear something?

09:14.754 --> 09:16.614
I have to look for her.

09:18.954 --> 09:21.684
Okay then. I'll help you!

09:23.124 --> 09:26.394
But I thought you were going to your teacher's.

09:26.694 --> 09:31.094
This isn't the time for that, is it?
Not after hearing such a terrible story!

09:32.104 --> 09:35.404
Anyway, how do you plan on looking for her?

09:37.374 --> 09:39.404
I know at least that she got off here,

09:39.404 --> 09:44.474
and that from that last station she took
the Nakayama Line going downtown.

09:45.944 --> 09:47.684
So I'll go around asking the station people if...

09:47.684 --> 09:49.874
No, no way! That'll never work!

09:58.324 --> 09:58.964
Looking for this girl
Karada Iokawa

09:58.964 --> 10:00.394
Looking for this girl
Karada Iokawa
Please help us!

10:00.394 --> 10:01.364
Looking for this girl
Karada Iokawa

10:01.594 --> 10:02.794
Thank you!

10:03.164 --> 10:04.654
Please help us!

10:05.204 --> 10:09.534
Kotomi, this is embarrassing!
You're taking things way too far!

10:09.534 --> 10:10.904
What're you talking about?

10:10.904 --> 10:14.114
This is your classmate, right?
Your friend, right?

10:14.114 --> 10:16.514
It's not the time for whining, right?!

10:16.974 --> 10:18.704
Please help us!

10:48.344 --> 10:51.314
PLEASE HELP US!

10:52.384 --> 10:56.244
PLEASE HELP US!

11:12.904 --> 11:14.994
Lunch is ready!

11:18.574 --> 11:21.164
Okay. Miss Sato?

11:23.074 --> 11:24.234
Yes!

11:30.624 --> 11:34.424
Well, we're lucky to have found
such a good employee.

11:34.424 --> 11:36.624
You're a hard worker, Miss Sato.

11:36.624 --> 11:38.614
No, I'm still learning.

11:39.424 --> 11:44.554
I have a knack for seeing whether or not
a person is worth their salt, you know.

11:44.834 --> 11:47.354
But not much talent for
running a business, hmm?

11:48.534 --> 11:51.104
I objected at first, you know.

11:51.104 --> 11:53.904
A couple of complete amateurs
suddenly opening up a bed and breakfast...

11:53.904 --> 11:56.934
But ma'am, your cooking is delicious!

11:59.044 --> 12:00.954
I'll show you a few things sometime.

12:00.954 --> 12:02.584
Thank you very much!

12:02.584 --> 12:05.574
That was actually one of the reasons
for starting a bed and breakfast:

12:06.454 --> 12:09.684
I just had to get your cooking to
as wide an audience as possible.

12:09.924 --> 12:11.724
My, such flattery.

12:11.724 --> 12:14.234
Still, that's assuming we actually
get some customers.

12:14.234 --> 12:16.664
I'm telling you, we're about to
enter the busy season!

12:16.664 --> 12:21.134
We'll get plenty of customers as people visit
here, reluctant to part with the fading summer...

12:21.134 --> 12:22.434
Right, Miss Sato?

12:22.434 --> 12:23.664
Y-yes!

12:24.104 --> 12:28.214
I'll go get us some coffee.
Are you all right with coffee, Miss Sato?

12:28.214 --> 12:29.774
I'll help!

12:29.774 --> 12:35.244
No, you rest a little while.
There's still lots left for you to do.

12:38.924 --> 12:40.114
Miss Sato!

12:48.964 --> 12:51.794
Human life comes from the ocean.

12:52.804 --> 12:55.604
Have you never heard that story?

13:00.674 --> 13:03.474
It's a folk legend from some
provincial town or other.

13:03.474 --> 13:04.544
Long ago...

13:04.544 --> 13:09.354
the people here believed that somewhere
beyond the sea lay the "mother world"

13:09.354 --> 13:12.514
from which all human life is brought.

13:13.184 --> 13:18.654
Thus, people are born when the tides come in,
and die when the waves recede.

13:19.624 --> 13:23.864
The people of old probably felt
that the ocean was their home...

13:24.364 --> 13:27.304
It's sort of romantic, don't you think?

13:30.674 --> 13:33.504
That's how he always is.

13:33.504 --> 13:36.634
He's laid-back, good-natured...

13:37.014 --> 13:42.214
And a starry-eyed dreamer I wish would
come down to Earth with me for once.

13:42.214 --> 13:44.854
It was a lovely story!

13:44.854 --> 13:47.084
The ocean bringing life...

13:47.084 --> 13:50.284
Oh, he knows all sorts of stories like that.

13:50.964 --> 13:52.924
He likes them.

13:52.924 --> 13:59.294
You know, he worked so hard, put up with
so much for the sake of our livelihood...

14:00.334 --> 14:05.004
That's why when it came to this,
I decided to let him do what he wanted.

14:05.874 --> 14:07.774
"Sure, I'll support you," I said.

14:16.414 --> 14:18.424
Looking for
Part-time Workers
Pension Isoka

14:18.424 --> 14:19.144
Looking for
Part-time Workers

14:29.394 --> 14:32.164
I left Hiro...

14:32.304 --> 14:35.664
and before I knew it, I'd arrived at this beach.

15:02.334 --> 15:04.024
I wonder how they're doing...

15:09.874 --> 15:11.334
Hello?

15:12.604 --> 15:13.704
Karada?!

15:13.704 --> 15:16.264
Where are you? Where are you now?

15:16.644 --> 15:18.164
Are you all right?

15:19.744 --> 15:20.974
Karada?

15:24.084 --> 15:29.924
Karada, listen! I'm really sorry I didn't
tell you about me and your brother.

15:29.924 --> 15:32.584
I want to talk to you. So...

15:34.934 --> 15:36.264
I...

15:37.634 --> 15:40.294
I'm all right.

15:41.374 --> 15:45.034
I'm getting by on my own. So please don't worry.

15:46.504 --> 15:49.234
Please tell that to Hiro as well.

15:49.674 --> 15:50.774
I'm sorry!

15:52.084 --> 15:54.044
Karada! Karada!

16:05.194 --> 16:07.664
Sasazuka
Pharmacy

16:14.104 --> 16:15.224
Welcome!

16:35.724 --> 16:37.524
Can I take your order?

16:52.344 --> 16:54.104
Well, why are we here?

16:56.244 --> 16:58.044
I got a phone call from Karada.

16:59.184 --> 17:02.204
She said she's doing well,
so not to worry about her.

17:02.984 --> 17:04.184
Where is she?

17:04.184 --> 17:05.654
I don't know.

17:06.384 --> 17:08.824
She called from a pay phone somewhere.

17:27.304 --> 17:29.204
I don't get it...

17:37.384 --> 17:40.014
I just don't get it.

17:42.024 --> 17:48.124
I'm not trying to evade the part I played in this,
but why did she leave?

17:48.394 --> 17:53.164
It's not as if knowing about our relationship
is enough reason for her to go running off.

17:54.374 --> 17:57.364
I mean, she's your sister.

17:59.174 --> 18:01.164
Say...

18:01.874 --> 18:07.244
Do you think she knew?
That she's not really your sister?

18:09.654 --> 18:12.244
She was with your parents
till she was eight, right?

18:14.024 --> 18:18.024
It's not hard to think that she realized
the truth somehow.

18:18.024 --> 18:20.464
Has there never been a sign
she might have known?

18:21.794 --> 18:24.064
Haven't you ever made sure?

18:26.664 --> 18:28.104
Why not?

18:31.444 --> 18:33.544
Because I didn't need to!

18:33.544 --> 18:36.474
Circumstances aside, we're brother and sister.

18:39.114 --> 18:40.584
You're running away, aren't you?

18:42.414 --> 18:44.854
You've been too scared to ask,
so you've avoided it.

18:44.854 --> 18:47.324
Telling yourself you'd probably
hurt her feelings...

18:48.224 --> 18:51.754
Why do you try to do things
by avoiding the truth?

18:53.124 --> 18:57.694
Why can't you understand what hurts people,
what you do to hurt them?!

18:58.334 --> 19:03.364
Sympathy? Empathy?! You think those
make a real brother and sister?

19:04.474 --> 19:05.904
Coward!

19:06.344 --> 19:07.634
Spineless coward!

19:08.174 --> 19:10.544
That's enough, dammit!

19:10.544 --> 19:12.744
I know you're worried about her, but...

19:12.744 --> 19:15.874
"Worried"?! I'm not worried at all!

19:17.954 --> 19:22.684
I miss her! She's gone, and I miss her!

19:43.514 --> 19:45.814
She's a relative of yours, right?

19:48.254 --> 19:52.014
I'm not going to start asking a lot of questions,
but I'll say one thing:

19:53.724 --> 19:57.884
My idiot of a brother is out there
searching for Karada.

20:05.004 --> 20:06.194
Thanks.

20:06.504 --> 20:08.974
Don't be so down in the dumps.

20:09.574 --> 20:12.564
If you keep working as hard as today,
you're sure to find her.

20:25.984 --> 20:27.424
Do you like her?

20:29.724 --> 20:31.354
Th-that's not what!

20:33.694 --> 20:34.824
Okay!

20:36.994 --> 20:39.834
What do you say we call it quits for today?

20:40.104 --> 20:43.794
If you don't hurry up and get home,
your mom will get angry at you.

20:45.644 --> 20:47.304
I'm not going back.

20:47.704 --> 20:50.804
I'm not going back until I find lokawa.

20:52.784 --> 20:55.944
That's sort of cool!

20:57.254 --> 21:00.524
But what's your plan for today?
Where will you stay?

21:00.524 --> 21:03.894
Uh-oh. I didn't think about that.

21:03.894 --> 21:06.464
I swear, you're just hopeless!

21:06.464 --> 21:08.524
Why don't you come with me?

21:09.534 --> 21:12.764
To my teacher's house!
I'm sure he'll let you stay, too.

21:13.534 --> 21:15.204
C'mon, let's do it.

21:15.204 --> 21:16.934
Uh, well. But...

21:16.934 --> 21:18.844
It'll be fine!

21:18.844 --> 21:23.744
Teach's place is on the Nakayama Line,
which makes it handy for looking for your friend.

21:23.744 --> 21:25.814
H-hang on! Kotomi!

21:25.814 --> 21:28.074
I'm telling you, there's nothing to worry about!

21:28.384 --> 21:29.954
Come on! Hurry, hurry!

21:29.954 --> 21:32.714
Hold on! Kotomi! My bag!

21:35.624 --> 21:37.024
Hello!

21:37.124 --> 21:39.024
I'm sorry I'm late.

21:40.024 --> 21:43.034
Kotomi! My, how big you've gotten!

21:43.034 --> 21:44.864
Oh, she's finally here, eh?

21:44.864 --> 21:47.564
It's been a long time, Mr. Isogai.

21:49.904 --> 21:53.804
This kid here is Amino, my old childhood friend.

21:54.404 --> 21:56.714
I sort of dragged him along.

21:56.714 --> 21:58.014
Uh, hello.

21:58.014 --> 22:00.534
Welcome! Please come in.

22:02.554 --> 22:05.144
Miss Sato! We have guests!

22:06.654 --> 22:08.024
Coming!

22:14.024 --> 22:20.264
Wearing unfamiliar shoes

22:20.264 --> 22:25.004
Each step a pain that I endure

22:26.444 --> 22:32.714
And yet I walk

22:32.714 --> 22:37.514
Because I have a place to return to

22:38.284 --> 22:46.424
I stare at myself

22:46.424 --> 22:51.024
And notice something I'd lost

22:54.164 --> 23:00.344
I want to be with you

23:00.344 --> 23:07.044
To feel it, near and far

23:07.044 --> 23:12.924
To keep creating each normal day

23:12.924 --> 23:19.564
With you, my beloved

23:19.564 --> 23:26.994
To say "I'm home,"
remove my shoes and hold you

23:27.234 --> 23:32.074
My sweet home

23:44.654 --> 23:47.744
A beach I once visited with Hiro.

23:47.884 --> 23:49.114
A path filled with memories.

23:49.254 --> 23:52.554
Beaches of white sand... Salty-sweet ocean air...

23:52.864 --> 23:58.164
Why have you come here?
Why, for my sake, would you?

23:58.564 --> 24:01.664
It's the first time I've felt such a thrill in my heart.

24:01.804 --> 24:05.204
But this heartache, could it be?

24:06.044 --> 24:07.504
Next time, on Living for the Day After Tomorrow:

24:07.504 --> 24:08.574
Next episode
The True Name
Next time, on Living for the Day After Tomorrow:

24:08.574 --> 24:10.244
Next episode
The True Name
"The True Name"

24:10.244 --> 24:12.214
Next episode
The True Name
